problem:
Problem description
- A factory produces a set $$\mathcal{P}$$ of products over a monthly planning horizon $$\mathcal{T}$$ using a set $$\mathcal{M}$$ of equipment types.
- Each product $$p\in\mathcal{P}$$ has a unit profit $$c_p$$.
- Each unit of product $$p$$ requires processing time $$a_{m,p}$$ on equipment $$m\in\mathcal{M}$$.
- Each equipment type $$m\in\mathcal{M}$$ has an available effective capacity $$u_m$$ during the planning horizon.
- The planning goal is to choose production quantities $$x_p$$ so that total profit is maximized while respecting all equipment capacities and making practical use of the available machine time.
- Business constraints:
  - Only products in $$\mathcal{P}$$ may be produced.
  - The total processing time required on each equipment $$m$$ by all produced products must not exceed the available capacity $$u_m$$.
  - Production quantities $$x_p$$ must be feasible output levels and cannot be negative.
  - The production plan should prioritize the mix of products that yields the highest total profit under the capacity limits.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_p$$: the planned production quantity of product $$p\in\mathcal{P}$$.
  - $$z$$: the resulting total profit of the production plan.
  - $$h_m$$: the total equipment time used on equipment $$m\in\mathcal{M}$$, if equipment utilization is reported.

Input Format
{
  "time_horizon": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{T}$$",
    "meaning": "monthly planning horizon",
    "structure": "single planning period"
  },
  "products": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{P}$$",
    "meaning": "set of products",
    "structure": "indexed set with size $$P$$"
  },
  "equipment": {
    "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{M}$$",
    "meaning": "set of equipment types",
    "structure": "indexed set with size $$M$$"
  },
  "processing_time": {
    "symbol": "$$a_{m,p}$$",
    "meaning": "processing time required on equipment $$m$$ for one unit of product $$p$$",
    "shape": "$$M\\times P$$"
  },
  "available_capacity": {
    "symbol": "$$u_m$$",
    "meaning": "available effective hours for equipment $$m$$ in the planning horizon",
    "shape": "$$M$$"
  },
  "unit_profit": {
    "symbol": "$$c_p$$",
    "meaning": "profit per unit of product $$p$$",
    "shape": "$$P$$"
  },
  "decision_variables": {
    "production_quantity": {
      "symbol": "$$x_p$$",
      "meaning": "quantity of product $$p$$ to produce",
      "shape": "$$P$$"
    }
  },
  "objective": {
    "symbol": "$$z$$",
    "meaning": "maximize total profit from all produced products"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "production_plan": {
    "symbol": "$$x_p$$",
    "meaning": "optimal production quantity for each product $$p$$",
    "shape": "$$P$$"
  },
  "equipment_usage": {
    "symbol": "$$h_m$$",
    "meaning": "total utilized hours on each equipment $$m$$",
    "shape": "$$M$$"
  },
  "total_profit": {
    "symbol": "$$z$$",
    "meaning": "maximum achievable total profit",
    "shape": "scalar"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "time_horizon": "1 monthly period",
  "products": ["I", "II", "III"],
  "equipment": ["A", "B", "C"],
  "processing_time": [
    [8, 2, 10],
    [10, 5, 8],
    [2, 13, 10]
  ],
  "available_capacity": [300, 400, 420],
  "unit_profit": [3, 2, 2.9]
}
